# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets — nothing in this block may ever reach GitHub.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Every env file, including .env.example. Real values live only on this
# machine and in the host's dashboard.
.env
.env.*
*.env
.envrc

# Key material of any kind.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.crt
*.cer
*.jks
*.keystore
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
*.asc
*.gpg
secrets.json
credentials.json
service-account*.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase — local CLI state and scratch SQL.
#
# Migrations are the exception and are tracked: they are the schema's only
# source of truth, they have to be applied in order, and a checkout without
# them cannot rebuild the database. They contain DDL and policies only — no
# keys, no connection strings, no data. Secrets live in the env files above,
# which are ignored wholesale.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/supabase/*
!/supabase/migrations/
.supabase/
.branches/
.temp/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dependencies
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/.next/
/out/
/build
/dist
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tooling / host state
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/coverage
.vercel
.netlify
.turbo/
.eslintcache

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor & OS noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
!.vscode/extensions.json
/.claude/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Logs
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Claude Design source canvases — self-unpacking bundles, ~500KB each, with
# fonts and images inlined as base64. Kept locally for reference; the design
# they encode lives in src/app/globals.css and the components.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/design/

# Claude Code plugin/skill caches and their scratch output. These are dropped
# into the project directory by installed skills, not written by this app.
.agents/
skills-lock.json
brag-output/
brag-output-*/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Video, and the working files that go with it.
#
# Promo and demo clips are generated into this directory by video tooling. They
# are large, they are regenerable, and they are not part of the app: nothing in
# src/ loads a video, and the only <video> this project would ever want is a
# hosted one. Ignored by extension as well as by folder, so a clip written
# somewhere new is still caught.
#
# This does NOT retract anything already committed. Git ignores untracked
# files only; a video that has been committed stays in history until it is
# rewritten out. Check with: git log --all --name-only | grep -i '\.mp4'
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.mp4
*.mov
*.webm
*.m4v
*.avi
*.mkv
*.prproj
*.aep
